// What a charted piece wears, beyond what lib/form's `Look` says of a place. A garment's piece
// has two faces and a cut edge, its patterns are drawn only as fine as a pixel holds, and its
// edges are inked as heavily as its look asks. Each is a function of the place, as the look is.
//
// (These belong with `form::look::Look` once lib/form takes them: a place's pixel footprint,
// a lining, a cut, an ink weight. Kept here meanwhile: docs/limbs.md, "What should move".)

use form::look::{Look, Place, Skin}

/// Where a piece is kept everywhere: far inside any cut.
pub const UNCUT: f32 = 1.0e4

/// A look a charted piece wears.
pub trait Worn: Look {
    /// What is worn at `at`, a pixel there covering `px` metres of the form at rest: a pattern
    /// finer than a few pixels is left out (it would shimmer).
    fn worn(self, at: Place, px: f32) -> Skin {
        self.skin(at)
    }

    /// Whether the piece's inside is seen as its lining where its back face shows at `at`. A
    /// piece that lies on another, whose inside can't be seen, shows its back face only edge
    /// on: as its outside, its normal brought round to the edge by the shading function.
    fn lined(self, at: Place) -> bool {
        false
    }

    /// What its lining wears at `at` (`at.normal` is the lining's own, out of the inside).
    fn lining(self, at: Place, px: f32) -> Skin {
        self.worn(at, px)
    }

    /// How far inside the piece's cut edges `at` is (m, on the form at rest; under 0 where it's
    /// cut away). Its edge is drawn where this is 0, as a line, so it is smooth across it.
    fn kept(self, at: Place) -> f32 {
        UNCUT
    }

    /// The weight of the line drawn along its edges (px).
    fn ink(self) -> f32 {
        1.0
    }
}
